1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,044
- [BILLY] <i>Hello?</i>
- [JORDAN] <i>Hey.</i>

2
00:00:03,128 --> 00:00:05,463
<i>I just called to check if you're okay.</i>

3
00:00:06,214 --> 00:00:07,048
<i>I'm okay.</i>

4
00:00:07,132 --> 00:00:09,551
<i>I don't want to add to your problems.</i>

5
00:00:09,634 --> 00:00:11,052
<i>I just found out</i>

6
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:12,971
<i>Bea got off the hook again.</i>

7
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:14,180
<i>What?</i>

8
00:00:14,806 --> 00:00:17,017
<i>Ms. Talia! Ms. Talia!</i>

9
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:19,394
<i>What are you doing here?</i>
<i>I thought you were in jail!</i>

10
00:00:19,477 --> 00:00:21,187
<i>I've done nothing wrong!</i>

11
00:00:21,271 --> 00:00:22,647
- [BEA] <i>Ms. Talia!</i>
<i>- Billy?</i>

12
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:25,567
<i>Bea's here, and she's making a scene.</i>

13
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:29,070
<i>I thought our plan would put her in jail.</i>

14
00:00:30,613 --> 00:00:33,575
<i>- Auntie Pres.</i>
<i>- Oh, Billy! I'm sorry.</i>

15
00:00:33,658 --> 00:00:35,410
<i>- I forgot to call you.</i>
<i>- It's okay.</i>

16
00:00:35,493 --> 00:00:38,204
<i>They said Sir Eric couldn't</i>
<i>come in to work today.</i>

17
00:00:40,749 --> 00:00:42,000
<i>Who paid for it?</i>

18
00:00:42,083 --> 00:00:43,752
<i>Your daughter did.</i>

19
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:47,255
<i>- She came here?</i>
<i>- Mm.</i>

20
00:00:47,338 --> 00:00:49,591
<i>You were asleep when she visited you.</i>

21
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:58,808
<i>The bill has been paid, but please,</i>

22
00:00:58,892 --> 00:01:01,561
<i>don't make me your emergency contact</i>

23
00:01:01,644 --> 00:01:05,106
<i>because next time, I won't be coming.</i>

24
00:01:06,357 --> 00:01:08,693
[PRECIOUS]
<i>Your father really is the worst.</i>

25
00:01:08,777 --> 00:01:10,695
<i>He even got you involved in his debts.</i>

26
00:01:10,779 --> 00:01:12,989
<i>I'm not surprised anymore, Auntie Pres.</i>

27
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:18,161
<i>When I found out that he became</i>
<i>a scammer in Canada,</i>

28
00:01:19,329 --> 00:01:22,123
<i>I already knew that</i>
<i>he was only after money.</i>

29
00:01:24,042 --> 00:01:25,710
[MARJ] <i>You're right!</i>

30
00:01:30,173 --> 00:01:32,008
[BILLY] <i>What are you doing here?</i>

31
00:01:32,091 --> 00:01:33,635
<i>Can you please talk to your people?</i>

32
00:01:33,718 --> 00:01:35,428
<i>Let the world know that I'm a criminal?!</i>

33
00:01:36,012 --> 00:01:37,680
<i>Do you think you're going to scare me?</i>

34
00:01:37,764 --> 00:01:40,141
<i>Enjoy your freedom</i>
<i>because it won't last long.</i>

35
00:01:42,393 --> 00:01:44,354
<i>Oh! And by the way…</i>

36
00:01:46,815 --> 00:01:49,317
<i>Orange looks good on you.</i>

37
00:01:55,657 --> 00:02:00,286
[BILLY] <i>They will officially provide us</i>
<i>our cybersecurity.</i>

38
00:02:01,287 --> 00:02:02,372
<i>Charm, what's wrong?</i>

39
00:02:04,457 --> 00:02:06,167
<i>Ralph's mom sent this.</i>

40
00:02:06,251 --> 00:02:07,710
<i>And now they're questioning me</i>

41
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:10,797
<i>if they did the right thing</i>
<i>when they invested in us.</i>

42
00:02:13,466 --> 00:02:15,135
<i>But what's worse is,</i>

43
00:02:15,635 --> 00:02:18,596
<i>they're questioning</i>
<i>my relationship with Ralph.</i>

44
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,473
<i>I thought you couldn't get to work today.</i>

45
00:02:20,557 --> 00:02:23,726
<i>By the way,</i>
<i>Billy wanted to give this to you.</i>

46
00:02:24,352 --> 00:02:28,731
<i>Actually, she's already been here twice,</i>
<i>but you just keep missing each other.</i>

47
00:02:30,650 --> 00:02:31,943
<i>Yeah, it's a shame.</i>

48
00:02:43,079 --> 00:02:44,164
[MARIELA] Have some, dear.

49
00:02:45,456 --> 00:02:47,959
It's so luxurious here.

50
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:50,879
The last time we ate at a place like this

51
00:02:50,962 --> 00:02:53,006
was when your sister Abi got promoted.

52
00:02:53,089 --> 00:02:55,925
And now, it's you.

53
00:02:56,009 --> 00:02:57,051
[CHUCKLES]

54
00:02:57,802 --> 00:02:59,596
That Billy thinks

55
00:03:00,179 --> 00:03:02,307
that she can just treat you
like you're nothing.

56
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:08,021
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

57
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:11,482
That's why I told you
to just trust me, Ma.

58
00:03:12,066 --> 00:03:14,319
Have faith in me.

59
00:03:27,624 --> 00:03:29,959
Did you just grimace?
Are you disgusted?

60
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:32,837
Why? Is it illegal to pick your teeth?

61
00:03:34,464 --> 00:03:37,175
Just pour me some wine

62
00:03:37,258 --> 00:03:39,052
before I run out of patience with you.

63
00:03:44,557 --> 00:03:45,934
That's it?

64
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:47,977
Come on, pour some more.

65
00:03:48,937 --> 00:03:51,147
What about you, Ma?
Pour some for my mom too.

66
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,233
Oh!

67
00:03:57,820 --> 00:03:59,197
- Okay.
- There we go.

68
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,657
- Thank you.
- Ma.

69
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:02,242
Cheers.

70
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:03,326
[SQUEALS SOFTLY]

71
00:04:03,409 --> 00:04:05,036
- Cheers.
- Cheers to…

72
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:08,039
us.

73
00:04:09,832 --> 00:04:11,084
Cheers.

74
00:04:11,167 --> 00:04:17,006
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

75
00:04:22,178 --> 00:04:23,263
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

76
00:04:28,351 --> 00:04:29,727
Eat more, Ma.

77
00:04:29,811 --> 00:04:31,145
- Here.
- You too.

78
00:04:31,229 --> 00:04:33,439
This. You dip it like this. Look.

79
00:04:35,525 --> 00:04:36,651
[BEA] Eat up.

80
00:04:45,243 --> 00:04:51,958
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

81
00:05:32,290 --> 00:05:34,167
I should be the one handling this, Ma.

82
00:05:34,751 --> 00:05:37,795
It was Benilda Cariño herself
who invited me out for dinner.

83
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:38,838
What?

84
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:41,299
Wait, I'm on my way.
I'm going to go there.

85
00:05:41,382 --> 00:05:42,425
[ROWENA] <i>Ralph, son.</i>

86
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:44,135
You're biased.

87
00:05:44,218 --> 00:05:46,929
<i>Okay? Your girlfriend works</i>
<i>for the company.</i>

88
00:05:47,013 --> 00:05:49,849
Let me be the judge
if you made the right choice

89
00:05:49,932 --> 00:05:52,185
in investing in this shady company.

90
00:05:52,268 --> 00:05:53,561
Shady?

91
00:05:53,644 --> 00:05:54,937
[RALPH] <i>What do you mean, shady?</i>

92
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:58,024
Ma, the legal issues
are not directly connected to LoveList.

93
00:05:58,107 --> 00:06:00,485
Then let me see for myself, okay?

94
00:06:01,069 --> 00:06:02,820
<i>I appreciate Billy's invitation</i>

95
00:06:02,904 --> 00:06:05,698
<i>so she could clear</i>
<i>her name and the company.</i>

96
00:06:06,282 --> 00:06:10,286
Now, I just want to know if the CEO
of LoveList is a decent woman.

97
00:06:10,369 --> 00:06:11,412
Ma.

98
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:13,539
Hello, Ma.

99
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:17,752
Ma, just wait for me outside.

100
00:06:17,835 --> 00:06:19,879
- I'm just going to settle the bill.
- Okay.

101
00:06:28,721 --> 00:06:30,264
Yes, ma'am? Can I help you?

102
00:06:30,348 --> 00:06:32,558
Ah, no. No, it's okay.

103
00:06:34,936 --> 00:06:41,275
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

104
00:06:52,203 --> 00:06:58,459
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

105
00:07:01,170 --> 00:07:02,964
- Hi, miss. Good evening.
- Hi, ma'am. Good evening.

106
00:07:03,047 --> 00:07:05,591
I have a reservation under Billy Cariño.

107
00:07:05,675 --> 00:07:07,510
[WOMAN] Your table will be
ready in a few minutes.

108
00:07:07,593 --> 00:07:09,679
- I'll just check your table.
- Okay. Thank you.

109
00:07:20,189 --> 00:07:22,191
Are you following my daughter?!

110
00:07:22,275 --> 00:07:24,360
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC STING]

111
00:07:27,363 --> 00:07:33,119
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

112
00:07:33,202 --> 00:07:34,662
Cat got your tongue?

113
00:07:35,204 --> 00:07:37,457
I'm not following your daughter.

114
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:39,584
You're trying to start a fight.

115
00:07:39,667 --> 00:07:42,044
Well, face me first.

116
00:07:43,171 --> 00:07:44,547
Excuse me.

117
00:07:46,883 --> 00:07:48,593
When will you leave my daughter alone?

118
00:07:48,676 --> 00:07:54,849
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

119
00:07:57,685 --> 00:07:59,896
Like I told you before…

120
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:05,735
it's your daughter you need to talk to.

121
00:08:08,988 --> 00:08:10,281
How dare you?!

122
00:08:13,159 --> 00:08:14,452
Not today.

123
00:08:17,371 --> 00:08:19,457
Ma. Ma!

124
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:23,294
Let go of my mother.

125
00:08:32,553 --> 00:08:34,263
- Leave my daughter alone!
- [BEA] Ma!

126
00:08:34,347 --> 00:08:36,015
- Ma.
- Karma will get you one day!

127
00:08:36,098 --> 00:08:37,266
I'll be waiting.

128
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:43,523
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

129
00:08:54,825 --> 00:08:56,702
Why did you stop me?

130
00:08:56,786 --> 00:08:59,121
I was ready to smack her face.

131
00:08:59,205 --> 00:09:00,456
She can't take both of us.

132
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,500
Shh. It's okay. It's done.

133
00:09:02,583 --> 00:09:05,002
Thanks, Ma. Thank you for defending me.

134
00:09:05,086 --> 00:09:07,296
But Billy is mine to handle.

135
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:08,881
I told you that, right?

136
00:09:08,965 --> 00:09:09,840
I'll handle her.

137
00:09:09,924 --> 00:09:11,717
But Caloy is gone.

138
00:09:13,177 --> 00:09:15,179
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

139
00:09:15,263 --> 00:09:16,264
Let's just go home.

140
00:09:21,018 --> 00:09:24,105
[WHEELS SCREECHING]

141
00:09:24,188 --> 00:09:25,356
Come on, let's go.

142
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:34,907
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

143
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:39,537
[BEA] Let's go, mister.

144
00:09:41,998 --> 00:09:45,418
Ms. Rowena, thank you so much
for taking the time to meet me.

145
00:09:45,501 --> 00:09:47,962
And I'm sorry about earlier.

146
00:09:48,045 --> 00:09:49,046
[SCOFFS]

147
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:50,881
- Don't be sorry.
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

148
00:09:50,965 --> 00:09:54,677
It just made me realize
that my instinct is never wrong.

149
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:59,432
My son made the wrong decision
to trust you and your company.

150
00:09:59,515 --> 00:10:01,517
With all due respect, ma'am,

151
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:04,937
I think your son made
a very wise decision.

152
00:10:05,021 --> 00:10:08,441
[LAUGHS]

153
00:10:08,524 --> 00:10:10,776
Based on what I saw earlier?

154
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:15,072
Again, I'm sorry you had to see that.

155
00:10:15,656 --> 00:10:19,619
It was a personal matter
that you should not have seen.

156
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:22,163
Maybe we can just focus on this instead?

157
00:10:22,246 --> 00:10:25,541
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

158
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:28,210
LoveList is up 42 percent

159
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:30,630
since we launched Happily Ever After.

160
00:10:30,713 --> 00:10:33,132
- Imagine what we can--
- Look.

161
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:36,594
I know you're doing this
because Charm is your friend.

162
00:10:36,677 --> 00:10:40,181
And while I admire you
for being a good friend,

163
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:42,767
I also need to be a good mother.

164
00:10:42,850 --> 00:10:45,895
I need to protect my son's well-being.

165
00:10:45,978 --> 00:10:46,937
Okay?

166
00:10:49,106 --> 00:10:51,651
- Billy. Billy, I'm sorry.
- [MOUTHS SILENTLY]

167
00:10:51,734 --> 00:10:53,402
It's okay. I'll handle Mama.

168
00:10:53,486 --> 00:10:56,155
No. It's not okay, Ralph.

169
00:10:56,238 --> 00:10:57,907
We're going to pull out.

170
00:10:57,990 --> 00:11:00,951
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

171
00:11:01,035 --> 00:11:02,411
We can't, Mom.

172
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:04,288
We can. It's covered under the morality

173
00:11:04,372 --> 00:11:06,749
and reputational risk clause
of the contract.

174
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:11,629
Okay. If that's the case,
I'm pulling out too.

175
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:15,091
From what? Our business?

176
00:11:15,174 --> 00:11:16,133
You can't.

177
00:11:16,717 --> 00:11:18,719
Your money is our money.

178
00:11:18,803 --> 00:11:19,720
No.

179
00:11:20,304 --> 00:11:21,347
From our family.

180
00:11:21,430 --> 00:11:23,724
All my life, I've just done
whatever you told me.

181
00:11:23,808 --> 00:11:25,601
And that ends now.

182
00:11:25,684 --> 00:11:28,187
- I'm already an adult!
- Then think like one!

183
00:11:30,147 --> 00:11:32,775
This company is not good for you,

184
00:11:32,858 --> 00:11:34,777
especially that girlfriend of yours!

185
00:11:34,860 --> 00:11:36,695
Excuse me, ma'am.

186
00:11:36,779 --> 00:11:39,615
I understand that
you're just looking out for your son.

187
00:11:39,698 --> 00:11:42,576
But have you tried
getting to know Charm personally?

188
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:45,413
Not just based on what you see
or hear from other people?

189
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:50,626
I hope you'll also give her a chance.

190
00:11:52,503 --> 00:11:53,921
This meeting

191
00:11:54,004 --> 00:11:55,339
is done.

192
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:58,426
Don't stay up too late.

193
00:11:59,593 --> 00:12:01,595
We have a board meeting tomorrow.

194
00:12:01,679 --> 00:12:07,893
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

195
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:09,019
[RALPH] Billy, I'm sorry.

196
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:10,521
[BILLY] It's okay.

197
00:12:11,188 --> 00:12:12,231
[RALPH HUFFS]

198
00:12:19,655 --> 00:12:21,449
At Ralph's age,

199
00:12:22,116 --> 00:12:25,619
I can't believe his mom
is still that controlling.

200
00:12:25,703 --> 00:12:28,497
Well, I'd rather have a controlling parent
than one who doesn't care.

201
00:12:29,999 --> 00:12:33,711
Not everyone has a parent
who worries about them.

202
00:12:34,795 --> 00:12:36,088
You have a point.

203
00:12:36,172 --> 00:12:37,214
But there should be a limit.

204
00:12:37,298 --> 00:12:39,884
Of course. But you know,

205
00:12:39,967 --> 00:12:42,887
she does all that
because she loves her son.

206
00:12:43,512 --> 00:12:45,473
Makes you wonder, what if…

207
00:12:47,057 --> 00:12:53,314
What if you had a mom
who was as protective as Ralph's?

208
00:12:53,397 --> 00:12:56,650
Or like Bea's mom.

209
00:12:57,276 --> 00:12:58,944
- Bea?
- Mm-hmm.

210
00:12:59,028 --> 00:13:03,782
I mean, didn't she come after me
because of her daughter?

211
00:13:06,076 --> 00:13:07,912
Bea's lucky to have a mom like that.

212
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:11,373
She's just unlucky
with her dad. He left her too.

213
00:13:14,376 --> 00:13:15,878
Thank you.

214
00:13:16,754 --> 00:13:18,047
[JORDAN] Mix it up first.

215
00:13:20,132 --> 00:13:21,383
This looks new.

216
00:13:24,762 --> 00:13:25,971
- Billy.
- [JORDAN] Charm.

217
00:13:26,055 --> 00:13:27,515
[BILLY] Charm.

218
00:13:27,598 --> 00:13:29,350
- Ralph.
- Brother.

219
00:13:29,934 --> 00:13:32,811
Billy, thank you.

220
00:13:32,895 --> 00:13:35,814
Because of you,
I finally came to my senses.

221
00:13:36,982 --> 00:13:38,776
Give him credit, Charm.

222
00:13:38,859 --> 00:13:41,028
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

223
00:13:41,111 --> 00:13:42,988
From now on,

224
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:44,448
I will decide for myself.

225
00:13:45,407 --> 00:13:49,995
Yes, but remember,
your mom is just worried about you.

226
00:13:50,079 --> 00:13:53,624
Our goal is for everyone
to understand each other.

227
00:13:53,707 --> 00:13:58,587
Remember what happened
with Melissa's dad and Theo?

228
00:13:59,171 --> 00:14:00,673
But you don't know my mom.

229
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:04,385
She'll do anything to get her way.

230
00:14:04,468 --> 00:14:07,555
Look, I've been a good son all my life.

231
00:14:09,431 --> 00:14:10,558
But now…

232
00:14:11,934 --> 00:14:14,353
Now, it's time for me
to be a better boyfriend.

233
00:14:15,646 --> 00:14:17,189
I need to make a stand.

234
00:14:17,273 --> 00:14:19,608
I don't care if she gets mad.

235
00:14:19,692 --> 00:14:22,820
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

236
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:24,238
Thank you, Ralph.

237
00:14:26,031 --> 00:14:27,491
[CHARM] But Billy's right.

238
00:14:28,117 --> 00:14:31,912
I just want all of us to get along.

239
00:14:32,997 --> 00:14:34,874
Your mother loves you, Ralph.

240
00:14:34,957 --> 00:14:37,543
She will meet you halfway.

241
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:40,421
That's what parents do…

242
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:47,761
I mean, most parents will do anything
for their kids, right?

243
00:14:47,845 --> 00:14:54,643
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

244
00:14:59,315 --> 00:15:02,484
["SUGAL" BY BRYAN CHONG PLAYING]

245
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:06,697
[CLAPPING]

246
00:15:08,741 --> 00:15:09,825
[BOTTLES CLINK]

247
00:15:15,873 --> 00:15:21,462
["SUGAL" CONTINUES]

248
00:15:23,881 --> 00:15:25,174
Give me my five hundred.

249
00:15:25,257 --> 00:15:27,968
Hey, hold on. We're not sure yet.

250
00:15:28,052 --> 00:15:29,428
Well, I'm sure.

251
00:15:29,511 --> 00:15:30,930
Not yet.

252
00:15:31,013 --> 00:15:32,890
Fine. If you say so.

253
00:15:34,308 --> 00:15:35,392
See?

254
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:37,019
That's your magic.

255
00:15:37,728 --> 00:15:38,979
You're like Cupid.

256
00:15:39,063 --> 00:15:40,147
Mm…

257
00:15:40,230 --> 00:15:42,358
That's why you're perfect for LoveList.

258
00:15:42,441 --> 00:15:44,109
[BILLY] Mm?

259
00:15:44,193 --> 00:15:47,237
[BILLY] Well, I'm not planning
to be Cupid.

260
00:15:47,321 --> 00:15:48,822
It's a hard job.

261
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:52,159
[BILLY] Do you remember?

262
00:15:52,242 --> 00:15:54,745
I created LoveList

263
00:15:54,828 --> 00:15:57,289
because I didn't want
what happened to me--

264
00:15:57,373 --> 00:15:58,248
To happen again?

265
00:15:59,124 --> 00:16:00,167
Mm-hmm.

266
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:01,502
And what happened to Mama.

267
00:16:04,213 --> 00:16:06,382
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

268
00:16:06,465 --> 00:16:07,758
Wait. Let's take a picture.

269
00:16:08,467 --> 00:16:10,302
I look a mess.
You should've taken it earlier.

270
00:16:10,386 --> 00:16:12,304
Come on, let's take one.

271
00:16:12,388 --> 00:16:13,263
Hmph!

272
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:16,934
- How do I look?
- You look fine.

273
00:16:17,017 --> 00:16:17,935
Teeth?

274
00:16:18,018 --> 00:16:19,019
- Don't worry.
- Okay.

275
00:16:19,103 --> 00:16:21,021
You're already beautiful. Hurry.

276
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:22,189
- Okay.
- Give me your phone.

277
00:16:22,272 --> 00:16:25,025
- Why my phone?
- The camera's better.

278
00:16:25,109 --> 00:16:28,153
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

279
00:16:28,237 --> 00:16:29,196
Ready.

280
00:16:32,741 --> 00:16:36,078
- Yay! They've made up.
- Cheers!

281
00:16:36,787 --> 00:16:39,289
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

282
00:16:39,999 --> 00:16:41,500
That angle makes me look bad.
One more time.

283
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:44,461
- [PHONE CHIMES]
- Oh, wait.

284
00:16:44,545 --> 00:16:45,754
- Who is this?
- Give it to me.

285
00:16:46,338 --> 00:16:48,424
You're too nosy! [CHUCKLES]

286
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:50,801
I've already seen it, so just tell me.
Who is it?

287
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:54,054
Someone I matched with on LoveList.

288
00:16:54,138 --> 00:16:56,348
- Mm-hmm.
- On LoveList?

289
00:16:56,432 --> 00:16:57,891
Mm-hmm.

290
00:16:58,475 --> 00:16:59,727
Is he bothering you?

291
00:17:00,310 --> 00:17:01,645
No, he's not bothering me.

292
00:17:01,729 --> 00:17:03,522
I would've blocked him already if he was.

293
00:17:04,398 --> 00:17:05,482
So,

294
00:17:06,608 --> 00:17:07,943
you like him?

295
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,987
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

296
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:11,071
Mm.

297
00:17:14,783 --> 00:17:17,953
- Mm.
- [JORDAN] Hmm…

298
00:17:21,749 --> 00:17:22,958
Is that really him?

299
00:17:23,667 --> 00:17:25,252
Maybe he's just a poser.

300
00:17:26,545 --> 00:17:28,380
Are you really working at LoveList?

301
00:17:28,464 --> 00:17:29,548
Yes.

302
00:17:29,631 --> 00:17:32,676
All the accounts on our app
are verified, remember?

303
00:17:33,761 --> 00:17:35,721
- Okay.
- Okay.

304
00:17:35,804 --> 00:17:36,847
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

305
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:38,849
Kris is a corporate lawyer.

306
00:17:38,932 --> 00:17:40,142
He graduated in the UK.

307
00:17:40,225 --> 00:17:42,936
He's 32 and already has his own law firm.

308
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:44,897
He likes to surf.

309
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:47,775
He has a younger brother
who's a freshman in college.

310
00:17:47,858 --> 00:17:49,026
How's that?

311
00:17:49,526 --> 00:17:51,487
- Wow.
- [BILLY] Wow.

312
00:17:51,570 --> 00:17:52,905
You know a lot about him.

313
00:17:55,365 --> 00:17:57,326
Are you really LoveList's tech lead?

314
00:17:57,993 --> 00:18:01,997
Obviously, I read all of it
on his profile.

315
00:18:04,124 --> 00:18:10,964
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

316
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:14,635
I thought you were busy.

317
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:18,680
So just because I'm busy, I can't date?

318
00:18:18,764 --> 00:18:20,015
Is it forbidden?

319
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:24,103
And weren't you the one who told me
I needed a distraction?

320
00:18:24,186 --> 00:18:25,479
- Yeah.
- Mm-hmm.

321
00:18:25,562 --> 00:18:28,816
If I do find love,

322
00:18:28,899 --> 00:18:30,818
I don't want to call it a distraction.

323
00:18:30,901 --> 00:18:34,404
He should support me more than anyone

324
00:18:34,488 --> 00:18:37,741
so I can stay focused on my goals.

325
00:18:37,825 --> 00:18:39,451
<i>Right? Right.</i>

326
00:18:39,535 --> 00:18:41,036
- Right.
- [BILLY] Mm-hmm.

327
00:18:41,578 --> 00:18:45,374
So, that guy is the one
you're talking about?

328
00:18:45,457 --> 00:18:46,875
[BILLY] Well, let's see.

329
00:18:47,793 --> 00:18:49,628
Why are you asking so many questions?

330
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:51,672
Are you a lawyer?

331
00:18:52,464 --> 00:18:53,507
Why not?

332
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:54,883
We don't know this guy.

333
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:56,885
Look, all I'm saying is,

334
00:18:56,969 --> 00:19:01,640
if you decide to go out
with this Kris guy or…

335
00:19:01,723 --> 00:19:03,183
- [BOTTLES CLINK]
- Easy.

336
00:19:03,267 --> 00:19:04,768
- …whoever.
- Mm-hmm.

337
00:19:05,644 --> 00:19:06,979
Just let me know.

338
00:19:07,646 --> 00:19:09,565
I'm ready to be

339
00:19:09,648 --> 00:19:12,067
your chaperone-slash-bouncer.

340
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:15,404
I'll think about it.

341
00:19:15,487 --> 00:19:17,197
- You don't want to?
- Mm.

342
00:19:17,281 --> 00:19:23,912
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

343
00:19:28,625 --> 00:19:30,210
[MUSIC FADES]

344
00:19:32,546 --> 00:19:39,511
["ABELYANA" BY MAKI PLAYING]

345
00:19:52,482 --> 00:19:58,113
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

346
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:24,890
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

347
00:20:39,905 --> 00:20:43,992
["ABELYANA" CONTINUES]

348
00:20:56,421 --> 00:20:59,341
<i>- Yay! They've made up.</i>
<i>- Cheers!</i>

349
00:20:59,424 --> 00:21:00,926
<i>- Wait!</i>
<i>- Who is this?</i>

350
00:21:01,009 --> 00:21:02,469
<i>You're too nosy!</i>

351
00:21:02,552 --> 00:21:04,680
<i>I've already seen it,</i>
<i>so just tell me.</i>

352
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:07,182
<i>Someone I matched with</i>
<i>on LoveList.</i>

353
00:21:09,851 --> 00:21:12,104
<i>Are you feeling ill, Jordan?</i>

354
00:21:12,187 --> 00:21:13,563
<i>A little.</i>

355
00:21:13,647 --> 00:21:18,110
<i>I don't know if it's right</i>
<i>to feel this way about Sir Eric.</i>

356
00:21:18,193 --> 00:21:20,821
<i>Don't you feel that way</i>
<i>about Brandon?</i>

357
00:21:20,904 --> 00:21:22,155
<i>No, this is different.</i>

358
00:21:22,239 --> 00:21:25,701
<i>Please give me a sign</i>
<i>if it's right to feel this way.</i>

359
00:21:25,784 --> 00:21:27,869
<i>You're up early, Ms. Supervisor.</i>

360
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:28,954
<i>Well, I have to.</i>

361
00:21:29,037 --> 00:21:30,539
<i>Do your best, dear.</i>

362
00:21:30,622 --> 00:21:32,332
<i>I will, like I always do.</i>

363
00:21:32,916 --> 00:21:34,084
[PHONE RINGS]

364
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:37,004
<i>Kris?</i>

365
00:21:37,087 --> 00:21:38,255
<i>Hi!</i> [GIGGLES]

366
00:21:38,338 --> 00:21:39,464
<i>Oh, you're near?</i>

367
00:21:39,548 --> 00:21:41,300
<i>Okay, I can meet you outside.</i>
